# The office writes .env for you. This shows what it can hold.
# With no DATABASE_URL, the office keeps its own Postgres in ~/.oddboro/db.
# Postgres in Docker on this Mac instead (`npm run db:up`):
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=pick-one
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://oddboro:pick-one@127.0.0.1:5432/oddboro
# Or hosted Postgres: the direct connection string from your provider.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host:5432/dbname?sslmode=require
# The office's time zone, for schedules and the clock. The first visit sets it.
# Until then the office uses this Mac's own zone.
# OFFICE_TIME_ZONE=America/New_York
# Staff and the office's drawing run on Opus unless the owner picks sonnet.
# OFFICE_MODEL=sonnet
# key: staff use the API key in the keychain instead of the Claude login.
# OFFICE_AUTH=key
# Odds that run on Grok use Grok's own default model unless this names one.
# OFFICE_GROK_MODEL=grok-4.7
# OFFICE_CODEX_MODEL=
# OFFICE_GEMINI_MODEL=
# The owner's answer to sending error and trace reports: yes or no. The
# office writes it when the owner answers. With no answer, nothing is sent.
# OFFICE_DIAGNOSTICS=no
# Where reports go. The app ships with New Altitude's address. A source build
# sends nothing unless you set your own Sentry DSN here.
# ODDBORO_DIAGNOSTICS_DSN=https://<key>@<your Sentry host>/<project id>
# Signing in to a New Altitude account goes to New Altitude's own site. For
# development only, this points it at another site, such as the test fake in
# apps/office/src/lib/server/fake-new-altitude.ts.
# ODDBORO_ACCOUNT_SITE=http://127.0.0.1:4598
